msgid "home.pricing.faq.headline"
msgstr "FAQs"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.runtime.question"
msgstr "In which cycle is a package booked?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.runtime.answer"
msgstr "The free trial version runs indefinitely.<br><br>All other packages have an expiration date.<br><br>If you decide to purchase a package on a monthly basis, you commit to paying for your package for at least one month. Your package will always run until the same day in the coming month.<br><br>The price of an annual package is also debited monthly. However, in this case you commit to paying for the package for at least one year. For this reason, you will receive a discount if you opt for the annual subscription.<br><br>The following is an example of monthly billing:<br><br>A monthly subscription with a billing cycle anchor on September 2nd will always be billed on the 2nd day of the month.<br><br>A monthly subscription with a billing cycle anchor date of January 31 will be billed on the last day of the month closest to the anchor date, i.e. February 28 (or February 29 in a leap year) and then March 31, April 30, etc."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.operation.question"
msgstr "What is a workflow operation?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.operation.answer"
msgstr "A workflow operation is an executed action in a workflow. Every action that is executed in the course of a workflow counts as an operation.<br><br>On the other hand, simply triggering a workflow or checking a condition does not count as an operation. Loop iterations are also not counted as workflow operations. However, every action that is executed in the course of a loop iteration is counted as an operation."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.organization.question"
msgstr "What is an organization?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.organization.answer"
msgstr "An organization is a structure that enables automation for a group of users and teams. Each organization has its own workflows, processes, databases, etc.<br><br>You can create teams in each organization to divide workflows, processes, databases, etc. into subgroups and thus restrict access."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.package.question"
msgstr "Where can I find information about the package I have booked?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.package.answer"
msgstr "You can find all kinds of information at any time on the package page of your account. There you have the option to upgrade and cancel your package. You can also see all the payments you have made and the limits and resources used for your package."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.upgrade.question"
msgstr "Can I upgrade my package?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.upgrade.answer"
msgstr "Yes, if the resources of your current package are no longer sufficient, you can upgrade it at any time on the package page.<br><br>If you have already booked another paid package, the price of the remaining time of the last month will be refunded as a percentage. This may take a few working days."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.downgrade.question"
msgstr "Can I downgrade my package?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.downgrade.answer"
msgstr "Unfortunately, this is not possible at the moment. Once you have a package, you can only upgrade to a higher package or the same package with a higher class. Unfortunately, it is not possible to downgrade.<br><br>Even if your paid package expires, you can only reactivate your account if you buy the same package or a higher one.<br><br>It is important to note that the private package of your account and the package of your organizations are to be considered differently. All these packages are independent of each other and can be upgraded independently. "
msgid "home.pricing.faq.termination.question"
msgstr "Can I cancel my package at any time?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.termination.answer"
msgstr "You can cancel your package at any time.<br><br>If you have booked a monthly package and cancel it, your subscription will be canceled immediately and you will not have to make any further payments. Your package will expire at the end of the current contract month.<br><br>If you have booked an annual package and try to cancel the package before the last month, the cancellation will be noted by our system but will not be executed immediately. Only when the contract year has expired will the cancellation be processed fully automatically and you will not be charged for the coming year. If you cancel your annual package within the last contract month of the year, the behavior is the same as a monthly cancellation."
msgid "home.pricing.faq.expiration.question"
msgstr "What happens after my package expires?"
msgid "home.pricing.faq.expiration.answer"
msgstr "In order for your package to expire, you must actively cancel it.<br><br>If your package has expired, you will lose access to all services on your account. You can reactivate your account within the first 6 months after your package expires by taking out the same subscription or a higher-value subscription.<br><br>If you have not resumed your subscription within 6 months after the expiry of your package, all your data stored with Dulno will be completely deleted. These cannot be restored. This includes all your workflows, processes, webhooks, databases, webhooks, devices and accounts.<br><br>If the booked package is an organization, the organization and all previously mentioned data will be deleted."

